This solution assumes that the "assert" conditions are in the form "@@@ some text". It is also assumed that the conditions will be correctly formatted (or that a good number of assumptions can be made based on the problem context).--------------------The Python solution would involve parsing the comments, extracting the requirements from them and adding assertions to the corresponding code. This is complex and would involve a good understanding of Python syntax and OOPS, but I will provide a simple python code to do a similar operation using regular expression:

```python
import re 

def extract_comments(string):
    regex = r'"""(.*?)"""|\'\'\'(.*?)\'\'\''
    regex_result = re.findall(regex, string, re.DOTALL)
    comments = [value for sublist in regex_result for value in sublist if value]
    return comments

def process_code(code):
    assert_statements = []
    lines = code.split('\n')
    for line in lines:
        line = line.strip()
        if line.startswith("### "):
            regex = r'\"#+\s+@@@\s+(.*)\s+###\"'
            match = re.match(regex, line, re.DOTALL)
            if match:
                assert_statements.append(match.group(1))
    return assert_statements

